. xttestpanel hausman

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Specification test: fixed vs random effects
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
H0: random effects estimator is consistent (cov(x, mu_i)=0)
classical = Stata's Hausman contrast; robust = Huber-weighted Mundlak test
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test                                              stat    df    p-val
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hausman chi2 (classical)                      392.0871     3   0.0000 ***
Robust weighted Hausman (Beyaztas)            272.9063     3   0.0000 ***
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Downweighted share of obs. = 19.0% (Huber tuning c=1.345).  Large gap between the two =>
influential/outlying obs.
Decision rule: reject H0 => prefer FE.  Refs: Mundlak (1978); Beyaztas et al. (2021).

